{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createDebouncedValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [CellValue<TValue>, SvelteDebouncer<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/svelte-pacer/src/debouncer/createDebouncedValue.ts#L36","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/svelte-pacer/src/debouncer/createDebouncedValue.ts:36"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derives a debounced value from its current source."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With the default trailing behavior, each call restarts the wait timer and only the latest pending update executes. Leading and trailing options control the edges."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns [value, utility]. The value is an accessor; call value() in the template. Pass a getter that reads reactive source state. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-and-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State and ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call during component initialization. Component destruction removes effects and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"source","children":[{"type":"text","value":"source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ValueSource"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/SveltePacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SveltePacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SvelteDebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SvelteDebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CellValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SvelteDebouncer.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SvelteDebouncer"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createDebouncedValue } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer'\n\n// During component initialization:\nlet source = $state('')\nconst [value, utility] = createDebouncedValue(() => source, { wait: 500 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value() for the committed value.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createDebouncer"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"state-and-ownership","text":"State and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"source","text":"source","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createDebouncedValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [CellValue<TValue>, SvelteDebouncer<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-pacer/src/debouncer/createDebouncedValue.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/svelte-pacer/src/debouncer/createDebouncedValue.ts#L36)\n\nDerives a debounced value from its current source.\n\nWith the default trailing behavior, each call restarts the wait timer and only the latest pending update executes. Leading and trailing options control the edges.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, utility]. The value is an accessor; call value() in the template. Pass a getter that reads reactive source state. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nCall during component initialization. Component destruction removes effects and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### source\n\n`ValueSource`\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`SveltePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/SveltePacerOptions.md)\\<[`SvelteDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/SvelteDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`CellValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`SvelteDebouncer`](../interfaces/SvelteDebouncer.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createDebouncedValue } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer'\n\n// During component initialization:\nlet source = $state('')\nconst [value, utility] = createDebouncedValue(() => source, { wait: 500 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value() for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\ncreateDebouncer\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createDebouncedValue\ntitle: createDebouncedValue\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createDebouncedValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [CellValue<TValue>, SvelteDebouncer<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-pacer/src/debouncer/createDebouncedValue.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/svelte-pacer/src/debouncer/createDebouncedValue.ts#L36)\n\nDerives a debounced value from its current source.\n\nWith the default trailing behavior, each call restarts the wait timer and only the latest pending update executes. Leading and trailing options control the edges.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, utility]. The value is an accessor; call value() in the template. Pass a getter that reads reactive source state. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nCall during component initialization. Component destruction removes effects and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### source\n\n`ValueSource`\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`SveltePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/SveltePacerOptions.md)\\<[`SvelteDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/SvelteDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`CellValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`SvelteDebouncer`](../interfaces/SvelteDebouncer.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createDebouncedValue } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer'\n\n// During component initialization:\nlet source = $state('')\nconst [value, utility] = createDebouncedValue(() => source, { wait: 500 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value() for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\ncreateDebouncer\n"}
